// Signing inputs for the macOS targets, indirected so the checked-in project
// builds without any certificate (CI, and contributors who have none) while a
// release machine gets a real identity without editing the project.
//
// To sign locally, write a Signing.local.xcconfig next to this file (it is
// gitignored) and set what you have:
//
//   WEBSPACE_TEAM_ID = 7NGC2P87LM
//   WEBSPACE_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
//
// The Mac App Store .pkg and the notarized Developer ID build are signed
// after the build by scripts/sign_macos.sh and need none of this. See
// docs/releasing-macos.md.

// The unsigned path. With no team, $(AppIdentifierPrefix) expands to nothing,
// so the app-group and keychain entitlements name no team: the app builds and
// runs, but flutter_secure_storage returns -34018 and the app group is
// unavailable. Good enough to develop against, never to ship.
WEBSPACE_TEAM_ID =
WEBSPACE_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
WEBSPACE_PROVISIONING_PROFILE =

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
